From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:13:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 238/260] [ae-patch] Tighten the bypass relaunch deadline and
 notices

The 70 s restart deadline now starts once the session lock is held, and a switch queued more than 15 s behind another answers a busy refusal without touching the pane. Any 504 from the runner path counts as an unknown outcome, not a refusal. The PATCH response carries permission_switch (switched, restarted or unconfirmed) so the composer says restarted only after a restart and shows a plain notice when the mode was not read.
